ent-ST14ClothingOuterArmorCombatVest = Mobile Infantry body armor
    .desc = Standard-issue armor of the Federation trooper. A single-piece chest plate made of flexible composite with a V-shaped ridge, with straps for gear and ammunition along the sides and bottom. Offers some protection against bullets but is nearly useless against Arachnid mandibles.

ent-ST14ClothingOuterArmorMedicalVest = Mobile Medical Infantry body armor
    .desc = Medical-pattern armor of the Federation trooper, marked with the corps cross. Lighter plating than the line trooper's kit so a corpsman can keep up with the squad.

ent-ST14ClothingBeltStandard = standard belt
    .desc = A plain webbing belt with pouches. Holds a trooper's odds and ends.

ent-ST14ClothingBeltEngineer = engineer belt
    .desc = A tool belt of the engineering corps, hung with loops and pouches for the gear a sapper needs.

ent-ST14ClothingShoesCombatBoots = Mobile Infantry boots
    .desc = Tall field boots of the Federation trooper. The grey fabric shaft with brown overlays is tightened by buckled straps, and the heavy sole has a deep tread. Worn with the full combat kit.

ent-ST14ClothingHandsGlovesCombat = combat gloves
    .desc = These tactical gloves are fireproof and shock resistant.

ent-ST14ClothingHandsGlovesEngineer = engineer gloves
    .desc = Insulated work gloves of the engineering corps. Fireproof and shock resistant.

ent-ST14ClothingHandsGlovesFingerlessCombat = fingerless combat gloves
    .desc = These tactical gloves are fireproof and shock resistant. The fingertips are cut away for fine work.

ent-ST14ClothingHeadCap = Mobile Infantry cap
    .desc = Grey service cap of the Federation trooper with a short visor. The winged Mobile Infantry emblem is embroidered on the front, with a diamond-shaped number patch below it.

ent-ST14ClothingHeadCapMed = Mobile Medical Infantry cap
    .desc = Grey service cap of the Federation trooper with a short visor, marked with the corps cross.

ent-ST14ClothingHeadCapEngineer = Mobile Engineering Infantry cap
    .desc = Grey service cap of the Federation trooper with a short visor, marked with the engineering corps insignia.

ent-ST14ClothingHeadHelmetCombat = M-3 tactical helmet
    .desc = Standard-issue helmet of the Federation trooper, made of the same flexible composite as the body armor. Covers the head and ears and is secured with a chin strap.

ent-ST14ClothingHeadHelmetMed = M-3 tactical medical helmet
    .desc = Standard-issue helmet of the Federation trooper, painted in corps colours and fitted with a medic's lamp.

ent-ST14ClothingHeadHelmetEngineer = M-3 tactical engineering helmet
    .desc = Standard-issue helmet of the Federation trooper, fitted with mountings for a welding visor and a head lamp.

ent-ST14JumpsuitInfantryUniform = Mobile Infantry uniform
    .desc = Field uniform of the Federation trooper - a padded grey jacket with black inserts and rank epaulettes, worn with reinforced-knee trousers. The winged Mobile Infantry emblem sits on the chest, with unit patches on the shoulders.

ent-ST14JumpsuitEngineeringUniform = Mobile Engineering Infantry uniform
    .desc = Field uniform of the engineering corps - a padded grey jacket with black inserts and rank epaulettes, worn with reinforced-knee trousers. The corps insignia sits on the chest.

ent-ST14ClothingBackpack = Mobile Infantry backpack
    .desc = The trooper's field pack. Grey composite shell with external straps for the rest of the kit.

ent-ST14ClothingBackpackSatchel = Mobile Infantry satchel
    .desc = A lighter shoulder bag for soldiers who do not need the full pack.

ent-ST14ClothingBackpackEngineer = engineer backpack
    .desc = The engineering corps field pack, with mounting points for a canister and a holstered sidearm.
